{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>Sheol</b> — that the generation of the cursers be cast into it and die before their time, as in: \"one who curses his father and his mother shall surely be put to death.\"" "<b>and the womb that shuts</b> — that the womb shut up, here meaning the belly, and they do not give birth, because of the generation that does not cleanse itself from the impurity of licentiousness, and he shall have no sons and shall have no seed." "<b>and the earth that is not sated with water</b> — when there is no rain, and arms dry up, and the lofty and exalted are brought low by famine." "<b>and fire</b> — it is that which descends from the heavens to consume the generation that devours the poor and oppresses the needy, as fire descended upon them in the days of Elijah, and likewise: \"and fire went out from before YHWH.\" Or the fire is an allusion to the heat that dries up, as when the rain does not fall, and he mentions father and mother a second time, for this deriding and cursing generation is worse than the three generations, and an eye that mocks the father who disciplines it and scorns the companion of the mother who disciplines it — may it be gouged out, and his eyes pecked out by ravines' ravens, who do not pity their young, and he shall not be gathered for burial, for the one who honors them will lengthen his days."], :book :proverbs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 30, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Proverbs -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/mishley/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:25:37.820258614Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}